  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Unique artist's book consisting of eight flattened tin cans the artist found in the streets of Rome. The cans are hinged to a steel cover held together with a steel clamp. The front cover features a crushed bottle top with "Non hai vinto"  (you did not win) printed on it. The spine title reads "La sconfitta del libro" (the defeat of the book). The artist references  two Futurist books created in the 1930s by F.T. Marinetti and others, constructed of tin sheets printed by the Litolatta company.</subfield>
  </datafield>
